# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bounding the subspace dimension for the latest version of Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"
msgstr "Membatasi dimensi subruang untuk versi terbaru Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bounding the subspace dimension"
msgstr "Membatasi dimensi subruang"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this walkthrough, we will show the effect of the subspace dimension in the [self-consistent configuration recovery technique](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068).\n"
msgstr "Dalam panduan ini, kita akan menunjukkan pengaruh dimensi subruang pada [teknik pemulihan konfigurasi self-consistent](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*A priori*, we do not know what is the correct subspace dimension to obtain a target level of accuracy. However, we do know that increasing the subspace dimension increases the accuracy of the method. Therefore, we can study the accuracy of the predictions as a function of the subspace dimension.\n"
"Specify the molecule and its properties.\n"
msgstr ""
"*A priori*, kita tidak tahu berapa dimensi subruang yang tepat untuk mencapai tingkat akurasi target. Tapi, kita tahu bahwa menaikkan dimensi subruang meningkatkan akurasi metodenya. Jadi, kita bisa mempelajari akurasi prediksi sebagai fungsi dari dimensi subruang.\n"
"Tentukan molekul dan propertinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate some random bitstrings to proxy QPU samples.\n"
msgstr "Bangkitkan beberapa bitstring acak sebagai proksi sampel QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Call SQD with increasing batch sizes.\n"
msgstr "Panggil SQD dengan ukuran batch yang makin besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This plot shows that increasing the subspace dimension leads to more accurate results.\n"
msgstr "Plot ini menunjukkan bahwa menaikkan dimensi subruang menghasilkan hasil yang lebih akurat.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension/extracted-outputs/caffd888-e89c-4aa9-8bae-4d1bb723b35e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension/extracted-outputs/caffd888-e89c-4aa9-8bae-4d1bb723b35e-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting an explicit bound with `max_dim` {#setting-an-explicit-bound-with-max_dim}"
msgstr "Menetapkan batas eksplisit dengan `max_dim` {#setting-an-explicit-bound-with-max_dim}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the sweep above, the subspace dimension was controlled only indirectly. `samples_per_batch` sets how many bitstrings are drawn into each batch, but the dimension of the resulting subspace is determined by how many *distinct* spin-alpha and spin-beta strings those bitstrings contain, and the pool of configurations available for subsampling grows from one configuration recovery iteration to the next. That is why the subspace dimensions on the horizontal axis above are irregular numbers that we did not pick.\n"
msgstr "Pada sweep di atas, dimensi subruang hanya dikendalikan secara tidak langsung. `samples_per_batch` menentukan berapa banyak bitstring yang diambil ke dalam tiap batch, tapi dimensi subruang yang dihasilkan ditentukan oleh berapa banyak string spin-alpha dan spin-beta *berbeda* yang ada di bitstring tersebut, dan pool konfigurasi yang tersedia untuk subsampling bertambah dari satu iterasi pemulihan konfigurasi ke iterasi berikutnya. Itulah sebabnya dimensi subruang di sumbu horizontal di atas berupa angka yang tidak beraturan dan tidak kita pilih sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `max_dim` argument of `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` bounds the dimension directly. It limits the number of CI strings retained in each spin sector, and since the subspace is spanned by the Cartesian product of the two sectors, its dimension is the product of the two sector dimensions:\n"
msgstr "Argumen `max_dim` pada `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` membatasi dimensi secara langsung. Argumen ini membatasi jumlah string CI yang dipertahankan di setiap sektor spin, dan karena subruang direntang oleh hasil kali Kartesius dari kedua sektor, dimensinya adalah hasil kali dari dua dimensi sektor tersebut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_dim=d` limits both sectors to `d` strings, so the subspace dimension is at most `d ** 2`.\n"
msgstr "`max_dim=d` membatasi kedua sektor menjadi `d` string, sehingga dimensi subruang paling besar `d ** 2`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_dim=(d_a, d_b)` limits the spin-alpha and spin-beta sectors separately, so the subspace dimension is at most `d_a * d_b`. When `symmetrize_spin=True`, the two limits must be equal.\n"
msgstr "`max_dim=(d_a, d_b)` membatasi sektor spin-alpha dan spin-beta secara terpisah, sehingga dimensi subruang paling besar `d_a * d_b`. Saat `symmetrize_spin=True`, kedua batas harus sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_dim=None`, the default, imposes no limit.\n"
msgstr "`max_dim=None`, yang merupakan default, tidak memberi batas apa pun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a batch contains more strings than the limit allows, the least important ones are discarded: the strings passed via `include_configurations` are kept first, followed by the strings carried over from the previous iteration (see `carryover_threshold`), and the remaining slots are filled with the sampled strings in decreasing order of how often they were sampled.\n"
msgstr "Ketika sebuah batch berisi lebih banyak string daripada yang diizinkan batas, string yang paling tidak penting dibuang: string yang diberikan lewat `include_configurations` dipertahankan lebih dulu, diikuti string yang dibawa dari iterasi sebelumnya (lihat `carryover_threshold`), dan slot yang tersisa diisi dengan string hasil sampling berdasarkan urutan menurun dari seberapa sering string itu disampel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because `max_dim` caps the size of the largest diagonalization that the eigenstate solver will be asked to perform, it is a convenient way to keep the solver within a runtime and memory budget: choose `samples_per_batch` generously, and let `max_dim` decide how large the subspace is allowed to grow.\n"
msgstr "Karena `max_dim` membatasi ukuran diagonalisasi terbesar yang akan diminta dari eigenstate solver, ini cara praktis untuk menjaga solver tetap dalam anggaran runtime dan memori: pilih `samples_per_batch` yang besar, lalu biarkan `max_dim` yang menentukan seberapa besar subruang boleh tumbuh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Below, we repeat the study, this time holding `samples_per_batch` fixed and increasing `max_dim`.\n"
msgstr "Di bawah ini, kita ulangi studinya, kali ini dengan `samples_per_batch` tetap dan `max_dim` dinaikkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The subspace dimension is now exactly `max_dim ** 2` in every run: it was chosen rather than discovered. Plotting both sweeps together shows that the accuracy is governed by the subspace dimension itself, whichever argument was used to arrive at it. The two curves need not coincide exactly, though. The `max_dim` runs draw 600 bitstrings per batch and then keep the most frequently sampled strings, so at a given dimension they can retain a better set of configurations than a run that reached that dimension by sampling fewer bitstrings in the first place.\n"
msgstr "Dimensi subruang sekarang tepat `max_dim ** 2` di setiap run: nilainya dipilih, bukan ditemukan. Memplot kedua sweep bersamaan menunjukkan bahwa akurasi ditentukan oleh dimensi subruang itu sendiri, argumen mana pun yang dipakai untuk mencapainya. Meski begitu, kedua kurva tidak harus persis berimpit. Run `max_dim` mengambil 600 bitstring per batch lalu mempertahankan string yang paling sering disampel, sehingga pada dimensi tertentu run tersebut bisa mempertahankan kumpulan konfigurasi yang lebih baik daripada run yang mencapai dimensi itu dengan mengambil lebih sedikit bitstring sejak awal.\n"

